Given the following entities, with `ChildA` and `ChildB` being sibling child entities of `Parent`, each child having separate relationships but with the same name `friends` only the relationship that is defined first gets used (i.e. in ChildA.friends is used on both ChildA and ChildB). This means that ChildB is shown to never have any related entities.

```ts
@Entity()
@TableInheritance({ column: { type: "varchar", name: "type" } })
export class Parent extends BaseEntity {

	@PrimaryGeneratedColumn()
	id: number

}

@ChildEntity()
export class ChildA extends Parent {

	@OneToMany(type => Friend, friend => friend.childA)
	friends: Promise<Friend[]>

}

@ChildEntity()
export class ChildB extends Parent {

	@ManyToMany(type => Friend, friend => friend.childB)
	friends: Promise<Friend[]>

}

@Entity()
export class Friend extends BaseEntity {

	@PrimaryGeneratedColumn()
	id: number

	@ManyToOne(() => ChildA, childA => childA.friends)
	childA: ChildA

	@ManyToMany(type => ChildB, childB => childB.friends)
	childB: ChildB

}
```

Calling the following results in the proceeding SQL query:
```ts
const a = await ChildA.findOne()
const b = await ChildB.findOne()
await a!.friends
await b!.friends
```

```sql
SELECT `ChildA`.`id` AS `ChildA_id`, `ChildA`.`type` AS `ChildA_type` FROM `parent` `ChildA` WHERE  `ChildA`.`type` IN (?) -- PARAMETERS: [["ChildA"]]
SELECT `ChildB`.`id` AS `ChildB_id`, `ChildB`.`type` AS `ChildB_type` FROM `parent` `ChildB` WHERE  `ChildB`.`type` IN (?) -- PARAMETERS: [["ChildB"]]

SELECT `friends`.`id` AS `friends_id`, `friends`.`childAId` AS `friends_childAId` FROM `friend` `friends` WHERE `friends`.`childAId` IN (?) -- PARAMETERS: [[1]]
SELECT `friends`.`id` AS `friends_id`, `friends`.`childAId` AS `friends_childAId` FROM `friend` `friends` WHERE `friends`.`childAId` IN (?) -- PARAMETERS: [[2]]
```

Notice how the last query, which should be accessing through the join table `friend_child_b_parent` uses the same query as `ChildA`. Is this perhaps just a limitation? I can make a test PR if it'll help.

